# TPV in PC + CDELT form with CDELT != 1. The TPV registry defines the
# polynomial on CD-matrix intermediate coordinates only; wcslib (dis.h,
# "Historical idiosyncrasies") applies TPV as a sequent distortion BEFORE
# CDELT, i.e. on PC*(p - CRPIX), and notes that the coefficients must then
# be scaled for the change of units. We follow wcslib. The coefficients
# here are in those pixel-like units (synthetic).
NOTE pipeline: TPV with PC + CDELT, polynomial applied before CDELT (wcslib)
GRID 1 2048 9 1 2048 9
PIX 1024.5 1024.5
HEADER
NAXIS   = 2
NAXIS1  = 2048
NAXIS2  = 2048
CTYPE1  = 'RA---TPV'
CTYPE2  = 'DEC--TPV'
CRVAL1  = 35.5
CRVAL2  = -4.75
CRPIX1  = 1024.5
CRPIX2  = 1024.5
CDELT1  = -7.3E-05
CDELT2  = 7.3E-05
PC1_1   = 1.0
PC1_2   = -0.0015
PC2_1   = 0.0016
PC2_2   = 1.0
PV1_0   = 0.3
PV1_1   = 1.0012
PV1_2   = -2.1E-03
PV1_4   = 3.0E-06
PV1_5   = -2.2E-06
PV1_7   = -1.0E-09
PV1_11  = 2.0E-10
PV2_0   = -0.2
PV2_1   = 1.0008
PV2_2   = 1.7E-03
PV2_4   = 2.5E-06
PV2_6   = -1.2E-06
PV2_10  = 3.0E-09
PV2_11  = -1.0E-10
